@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.2.2
@changelog
  - Codename: Trust me - I know what I'm doing!
  - New: Bus-Compressor favourites alongside Channel-Strip favourites — same 8-slot Switch / Cycle / Copy model on its own domain
  - New: named favourite Sets with separate CS and BC libraries, assignable per track (one CS + one BC set); tracks with no set use the Base bank
  - New: Copy vs Own settings per domain when switching/cycling a favourite (CS defaults Copy, BC defaults Own); per-favourite + per-track settings memory keyed by plug-in identity
  - New: Copy-to-CS-N (A/B) inserts a favourite below the active strip with values carried and the original bypassed, with a per-section copy mask (EQ / Dyn / Gate / Fader)
  - New: unified domain-aware Switch / Copy / Cycle to Favourite N actions + one Favourites soft-key bank
  - New: UC1 favourite-cycle carousel (prev / current / next), left encoder = CS, right = BC
  - Fix: send & receive faders now record automation (volume + pan) in Touch / Write / Latch — previously CSurf writes did not record reliably; now via the correct UI path, and the surface follows recorded send automation and snaps back on Touch release
  - New: additive Settings search — space-separated words in any order (e.g. "favo focu" finds "Favourite ... Focused")
  - Fix: with "Parameter change switches soft-key bank" off, a soft-key press fires the bank its labels show (no label/dispatch mismatch); send-pan readout shows the send's effective pan
